Z||000000||maryjane||09-01-2001||07:25 PM||||This was passed along to me so I thought I would share it if anyone doesn't already know.<BR>If your credit cards are stolen, first and immediately cancel the cards.<BR>Keep the tollfree # to the credit companies handy so you can quickly advise them of the theft. Most thieves use the cards quickly, so there is no time to waste.<BR>File a police report in the jurisdiction the theft occured.(it proves to the credit companies that you were diligent.) and is a first step to an investigation (if there ever is one)<BR>Call the three national credit reporting companies asap to place a fraud alert on the cards stolen and your SS#.(this part may cause some short term grief, but will help in the long term) The #'s are:<BR>Equifax: 1-800-525-6285<BR>Experian (formerly TRW):1-888-397-3742<BR>Trans Union: 1-800-680-7289<BR>Social Scurity Administration (frad line):1-800-269-0271||||reg||1
